WEBVTT

00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.319
The Irresponsible Captain
Tylor

00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:11.958
We may be off the maps...
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:11.958 --> 00:00:14.017
...but let's stay on this voyage.
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:14.861 --> 00:00:18.991
I will be holding, never let you go.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.403
Whatever we may want...
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:23.403 --> 00:00:25.530
...we'll take as we need.
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:26.306 --> 00:00:30.333
So let's just go wherever we please!
Omoi no Mama Yukou!

00:00:32.045 --> 00:00:34.814
Make me your partner...
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:34.814 --> 00:00:37.442
...on this journey.
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:41.312
One that you trust more than words!
Michizure ni Shite

00:00:42.756 --> 00:00:47.420
Come on now and sail away for future!
Imasugu sail away for future

00:00:48.428 --> 00:00:49.929
Things are waiting...
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:53.126
...that we've never seen before!
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:57.137
Just take your cares...
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:00:57.137 --> 00:01:01.198
...and throw them all away.
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:01:01.441 --> 00:01:06.071
Come together, just think of tomorrow.

00:01:07.847 --> 00:01:09.337
Let's go!

00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:15.984
THE SHIP SETS SAIL,
BUT MISGIVINGS REMAIN

00:01:22.595 --> 00:01:24.654
All right!
I've got my chance!

00:01:25.432 --> 00:01:26.330
What the?

00:01:26.599 --> 00:01:29.090
Let's go!
To the ends of space!

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.538
Lieutenant Yamamoto, I have
a feeling this new posting...

00:01:40.613 --> 00:01:42.547
...will be a great
ordeal for you...

00:01:42.615 --> 00:01:45.641
...but I've every
expectation you'll do well.

00:01:46.486 --> 00:01:51.219
Yes, sir! As a humble member of
the United Planets Space Force...

00:01:51.291 --> 00:01:55.091
...I stand ready to
destroy the Raalgon menace!

00:01:55.195 --> 00:01:59.188
I'm sure. However, the enemy
to fear is not the Raalgon.

00:01:59.399 --> 00:01:59.956
Sir?

00:02:00.633 --> 00:02:01.600
The enemy...

00:02:03.136 --> 00:02:04.569
The enemy lies within.

00:02:06.272 --> 00:02:06.931
Within?

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.307
The enemy lies within!

00:02:12.946 --> 00:02:14.914
Ladies and gentlemen of
the destroyer Soyokaze...

00:02:14.981 --> 00:02:17.450
...as I take on the duties
of first officer here...

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.748
...I wanted you to
hear those words!

00:02:20.353 --> 00:02:24.891
The enemy lies within! Those words
were said by Admiral Mifune...

00:02:24.891 --> 00:02:27.052
...the commander of the
outer galactic fleet.

00:02:27.327 --> 00:02:30.262
I'm sure you can understand
the meaning of those words.

00:02:31.731 --> 00:02:33.062
The enemy within...

00:02:33.666 --> 00:02:38.035
It is the weak heart within
us which fears death.

00:02:38.538 --> 00:02:42.474
A soldier must not fear
death on the battlefield!

00:02:42.876 --> 00:02:45.538
Talks big for a greenhorn.

00:02:45.612 --> 00:02:49.013
Don't be rude, Cryburn. He IS the
first officer... For now, at least.

00:02:49.649 --> 00:02:54.643
Dropship pilot Andressen
and the Marines...

00:02:55.155 --> 00:02:58.358
Bear in mind that
proper decorum...

00:02:58.358 --> 00:03:01.293
...is the mark of a
true UPSF soldier!

00:03:01.628 --> 00:03:08.329
I expect your attitudes to improve
before the new captain arrives!

00:03:09.969 --> 00:03:14.338
It'll be fun knocking him off
that high horse. Right, Skipper?

00:03:19.979 --> 00:03:23.779
I still can't believe
you're both coming with me.

00:03:24.184 --> 00:03:27.176
But you saved our
father's life, Mr. Tylor.

00:03:27.253 --> 00:03:30.689
It's just natural we'd want
to repay your kindness.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.916
But there's two of you
and only one of me.

00:03:34.761 --> 00:03:36.991
It'll get to be
too much eventually.

00:03:37.263 --> 00:03:39.891
Oh, Mr. Tylor! There it is!

00:03:39.999 --> 00:03:41.626
There's the Soyokaze!

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.325
Oh? Where? Where?

00:03:47.807 --> 00:03:48.899
Oh, my...

00:03:53.546 --> 00:03:55.639
You mean that junk heap?

00:03:55.982 --> 00:03:58.075
These are the
designated coordinates.

00:03:58.284 --> 00:04:00.486
Ship's transponder code checks out.

00:04:00.486 --> 00:04:02.420
That's definitely
the destroyer Soyokaze.

00:04:03.122 --> 00:04:06.353
Soyokaze - "The Gentle Breeze"

00:04:06.593 --> 00:04:09.153
Above all, the captain is the
very embodiment of the ship!

00:04:09.462 --> 00:04:11.123
That is what I believe!

00:04:11.798 --> 00:04:14.198
If he tells you to die,
you should do so happily!

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:19.295
I, your first officer, expect you
all to believe this ideal as I do!

00:04:19.439 --> 00:04:23.933
For he is the captain,
and he's earned that title!

00:04:25.445 --> 00:04:27.276
This way, Mr. Tylor!

00:04:30.283 --> 00:04:31.375
Hi. What's up?

00:04:32.852 --> 00:04:34.979
Well, well. Everyone's here.

00:04:36.656 --> 00:04:39.557
Oh, Lieutenant Yamamoto.
It's been a while.

00:04:39.659 --> 00:04:42.628
Did they assign you to this
broken-down destroyer, too?

00:04:43.129 --> 00:04:45.654
You! You're that guy
from the pension department!

00:04:46.299 --> 00:04:49.564
Well, what do you know?
If it isn't Yuriko!

00:04:50.003 --> 00:04:52.267
So, what brings you
to this junk heap?

00:04:52.639 --> 00:04:54.004
Please don't touch me.

00:04:55.141 --> 00:04:56.768
I see you haven't changed.

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:59.103
But I still think you're
beautiful when you're angry.

00:04:59.178 --> 00:05:00.509
Why are you here?!

00:05:01.481 --> 00:05:04.183
What's a recruit from the pension
department doing on this ship?!

00:05:04.183 --> 00:05:07.209
Oh, come on!
To work, of course.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.014
Work? You mean?

00:05:10.823 --> 00:05:13.656
I've been assigned
to this ship, too.

00:05:14.994 --> 00:05:17.690
Although I was sorta surprised
to see what a wreck it is.

00:05:17.797 --> 00:05:23.201
I see... Then you'd better
be sure to follow my orders.

00:05:23.269 --> 00:05:24.031
Why?

00:05:24.437 --> 00:05:27.167
Because I am the
Soyokaze's first officer.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.567
Really? No kidding? Well, do
a good job, Lieutenant Yamamoto.

00:05:32.278 --> 00:05:36.305
Until the new captain arrives,
I am the ship's acting captain.

00:05:36.716 --> 00:05:41.119
Meaning I have the highest
authority on board, so...

00:05:41.187 --> 00:05:44.452
Well, in that case, you can
stop being acting captain now.

00:05:44.524 --> 00:05:45.422
Good work!

00:05:45.958 --> 00:05:47.585
What do you mean?

00:05:48.027 --> 00:05:49.221
Umm...

00:05:50.563 --> 00:05:51.257
Here you go!

00:05:52.932 --> 00:05:58.461
Justy Ueki Tylor, as of 1 April
UC 6998, is reassigned from...

00:05:58.538 --> 00:06:00.631
...the pension department
of benefits administration...

00:06:01.474 --> 00:06:03.743
...advanced to the rank
of lieutenant commander...

00:06:03.743 --> 00:06:05.370
...and is assigned to the
destroyer Soyokaze as...

00:06:06.879 --> 00:06:12.010
As the Soyokaze's captain?!

00:06:12.518 --> 00:06:13.542
You got it.

00:06:16.222 --> 00:06:20.215
There must be some mistake!
This is insane!

00:06:20.693 --> 00:06:22.456
You seem sorta surprised.

00:06:23.129 --> 00:06:28.401
You see, when I saved Yuriko,
Emi, and Yumi that time...

00:06:28.401 --> 00:06:30.570
...the senior staff thought
it was pretty heroic.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:31.730
That's right!

00:06:34.207 --> 00:06:36.175
I'm afraid it's true.

00:06:42.815 --> 00:06:46.478
In short, I'm Lieutenant Commander
Tylor, the captain of this ship!

00:06:46.619 --> 00:06:50.612
People, let's all work really
hard and win this war!

00:06:53.192 --> 00:06:54.784
This is freakin' PERFECT!

00:06:55.294 --> 00:07:00.561
You gonna happily die when he
tells you to, Lieutenant, sir?

00:07:17.784 --> 00:07:20.275
Thanks, I'm feeling
much better now.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:24.014
I never knew how effective
neuro-cleansing was.

00:07:24.223 --> 00:07:28.125
I find this method is
much more effective for me.

00:07:31.597 --> 00:07:33.394
Care for a drink, Lieutenant?

00:07:33.733 --> 00:07:35.132
Uh, no, thanks.

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:40.237
I'm surprised how well you can
work when you're so drunk.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:45.343
It's nothing. I've been doing
this for thirty years, after all.

00:07:45.878 --> 00:07:47.846
Oh? Thirty years?

00:07:48.514 --> 00:07:51.677
You must have saved the
lives of many soldiers.

00:07:53.352 --> 00:07:56.412
Don't be ridiculous!
I'm only thirty-three years old.

00:07:56.789 --> 00:07:58.882
I was talking about
my drinking habit.

00:07:59.659 --> 00:08:00.353
Huh?

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.988
Uh-oh, if I keep up this pace,
I'll run out before we get back.

00:08:32.024 --> 00:08:32.581
Hi!

00:08:42.702 --> 00:08:45.296
Chief Helmsman,
Lt. j.g. Harold Katori!

00:08:45.771 --> 00:08:47.102
Yes, Captain! Can I help you?

00:08:48.307 --> 00:08:49.467
Just checking.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:53.778
Communications Officer,
Lt. j.g. Kyon-Hwa Kim!

00:08:54.113 --> 00:08:55.011
Yes, Captain?

00:08:56.682 --> 00:08:57.944
Just checking again.

00:09:02.722 --> 00:09:05.418
Intelligence Officer,
Lt. Cmdr. Yuriko Star!

00:09:05.858 --> 00:09:08.827
Please do not call me unless
you have something for me to do.

00:09:09.362 --> 00:09:11.091
But I do have
some work for you.

00:09:11.797 --> 00:09:15.927
Could you call up navigation
data on the surrounding sectors?

00:09:17.537 --> 00:09:20.734
As soon as we're ready,
we're setting sail.

00:09:20.907 --> 00:09:24.934
Captain, we need clearance
from HQ to leave port.

00:09:25.211 --> 00:09:27.042
Oh, never mind the rules.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:31.243
Sir, if we do that, it'll be a
serious breach of regulations.

00:09:31.651 --> 00:09:33.185
They won't let you off
with just confinement...

00:09:33.185 --> 00:09:37.053
Pardon me! Question here!
Who do you obey on a ship?

00:09:37.757 --> 00:09:39.892
Well, the captain,
of course, but...

00:09:39.892 --> 00:09:43.453
Exactly! Now that that's
settled, let's move out!

00:09:49.235 --> 00:09:50.702
Attention, all hands!

00:09:51.137 --> 00:09:52.832
Emergency orders
from the captain!

00:09:53.539 --> 00:09:55.905
All hands report to stations!

00:09:56.542 --> 00:09:58.203
Prep for emergency launch!

00:10:24.503 --> 00:10:25.492
We're moving!

00:10:25.972 --> 00:10:27.907
In complete disregard of
headquarters' operation orders...

00:10:27.907 --> 00:10:29.942
...and my position
as first officer!

00:10:29.942 --> 00:10:31.341
This ship! This ship!

00:10:35.247 --> 00:10:39.149
THIS SHIP IS MOVING!!!

00:10:57.136 --> 00:10:59.434
Take care of things
on your end, Skipper.

00:11:00.172 --> 00:11:03.300
We Marines have
a little job to do.

00:11:03.843 --> 00:11:06.835
For God's sake... ANOTHER
rumble with the pilots?

00:11:08.047 --> 00:11:09.810
Can't say I see
what the cause is.

00:11:09.882 --> 00:11:14.012
Why do you Marines fight
with the pilots so much?

00:11:15.321 --> 00:11:19.155
'Cuz it's harder
to fight tradition.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:37.903
Hang on, baby... You'll be
tearing through space real soon.

00:11:45.751 --> 00:11:47.218
He's so irresponsible!

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:51.813
If we don't contact HQ soon,
we'll really be in trouble.

00:11:52.458 --> 00:11:56.758
As long as I'm at the helm,
this ship's as safe as a cradle.

00:11:57.663 --> 00:11:59.995
Pretty sure of yourself,
aren't you, Lieutenant Katori?

00:12:00.933 --> 00:12:02.298
I'm just stating a fact.

00:12:03.102 --> 00:12:06.094
Maybe you're the
perfect helmsman for Tylor.

00:12:06.539 --> 00:12:10.209
Lieutenant Kim, didn't you
forget the "captain" on his name?

00:12:10.209 --> 00:12:12.871
Who cares?
Tylor's in dreamland...

00:12:13.112 --> 00:12:15.444
...and the first officer's
confined himself to his quarters.

00:12:15.781 --> 00:12:20.081
As long as we don't run into a
Raalgon ship, I'm perfectly happy.

00:12:31.831 --> 00:12:35.562
I'm not afraid of
dying on the battlefield.

00:12:35.935 --> 00:12:40.838
But I refuse to die uselessly on the
orders of an incompetent commander!

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:45.977
Why?! Why did the military
promote that man above me?!

00:12:50.216 --> 00:12:53.344
"To First Officer Yamamoto,
from the veterans..."

00:12:54.353 --> 00:12:56.913
I see... I see now!

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:00.659
They're UPSF soldiers
through and through!

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:03.827
They may be a bit insolent,
but their hearts are pure.

00:13:05.965 --> 00:13:08.267
Even if the captain
is irresponsible...

00:13:08.267 --> 00:13:10.758
...I have to carry on,
for their sake.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:22.711
Why me?

00:13:26.519 --> 00:13:29.852
Anyway, make sure the captain
opens it when he wakes up.

00:13:30.356 --> 00:13:31.015
Sure thing.

00:13:43.068 --> 00:13:44.592
I shot them all down!

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:46.863
Hmm... Not bad, little lady.

00:13:47.473 --> 00:13:51.432
But real battles
aren't like flight sims.

00:13:52.178 --> 00:13:54.914
Ensign Kojiro here
may act like a veteran...

00:13:54.914 --> 00:13:57.075
...but he hasn't even
logged a thousand hours yet.

00:13:57.183 --> 00:13:58.707
Don't let him intimidate you.

00:13:59.485 --> 00:14:01.887
Someone with no talent can fly
tens of thousands of hours...

00:14:01.887 --> 00:14:03.878
...and still never be good.
Understand?

00:14:04.089 --> 00:14:07.354
All that matters
for a pilot is natural ability.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:12.158
When I sit in the cockpit,
the plane becomes a part of me.

00:14:12.431 --> 00:14:15.992
Big words for a stinkin' flyboy!

00:14:22.208 --> 00:14:26.668
This Hammer lets me smash an enemy
with my fists! It's a real weapon!

00:14:26.812 --> 00:14:29.679
Oh, I see. It's perfect
for barbarians like you!

00:14:30.015 --> 00:14:31.209
How sweet!

00:14:34.653 --> 00:14:38.991
Listen, greenhorn, you'd
just better remember that...

00:14:38.991 --> 00:14:44.725
...aboard the Soyokaze,
you pilots work for us Marines!

00:14:45.731 --> 00:14:47.756
And what if I say
I don't agree with you?

00:14:52.771 --> 00:14:53.999
You son of a!

00:14:56.242 --> 00:14:56.936
Eat this!

00:15:03.215 --> 00:15:04.216
Oh, yeah?!

00:15:04.216 --> 00:15:05.979
Darn it, lemme go!

00:15:06.919 --> 00:15:07.715
Why, that!

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:19.598
What do we do?!
What do we do?!

00:15:20.432 --> 00:15:22.059
Let's tell Captain Tylor.

00:15:26.438 --> 00:15:28.963
Damn them all... Monsters!

00:15:29.308 --> 00:15:32.175
How dare they do this!
I'll make them pay!

00:15:34.446 --> 00:15:35.743
Cmdr. Yuriko Star...

00:15:36.448 --> 00:15:38.541
I thought something
like this would happen.

00:15:39.051 --> 00:15:40.519
They did it, right?

00:15:40.519 --> 00:15:43.756
Those! I'll have
them court-martialed...

00:15:43.756 --> 00:15:46.850
...and drummed out of the
United Planets Space Force!

00:15:47.226 --> 00:15:48.818
You mustn't do that,
Lieutenant Yamamoto!

00:15:50.462 --> 00:15:52.765
If you lose your cool now...

00:15:52.765 --> 00:15:55.199
...the crew of the Soyokaze
really will be doomed.

00:15:55.734 --> 00:15:58.100
Commander Star,
what are you saying?

00:15:58.304 --> 00:16:02.832
I came aboard this
ship to reform the crew.

00:16:04.977 --> 00:16:08.572
What decided that
for me was Captain Tylor.

00:16:09.148 --> 00:16:11.378
Or, rather,
before he became captain.

00:16:13.419 --> 00:16:15.887
Besides risking his life
to save Admiral Hanner...

00:16:16.422 --> 00:16:20.756
...he resolved that crisis peacefully
and allowed the military to save face.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:23.827
So it was only natural the high
command wanted to promote him.

00:16:24.363 --> 00:16:28.663
But Admiral Mifune saw Tylor
for what he really was.

00:16:28.834 --> 00:16:33.771
This man may be a member of the
UPSF, but he is not one of us!

00:16:33.973 --> 00:16:37.943
If we carelessly entrust him with
the responsibilities of a soldier...

00:16:37.943 --> 00:16:40.779
...it's clear to me that he'll
make some horrible mistake...

00:16:40.779 --> 00:16:43.942
...and throw our
forces into chaos.

00:16:45.684 --> 00:16:48.287
As you know, the Soyokaze...

00:16:48.287 --> 00:16:51.256
...is considered the
dumping ground of the UPSF.

00:16:52.091 --> 00:16:56.323
Its crew have always just been
outlaws from all over space.

00:16:56.962 --> 00:17:00.557
No new captain has ever
lasted more than three days.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:05.237
So Admiral Mifune decided to make
Tylor the Soyokaze's captain...

00:17:05.237 --> 00:17:09.640
...so he could later be able to
throw him out of the military.

00:17:10.409 --> 00:17:12.809
But, then, why are you here?

00:17:13.145 --> 00:17:16.478
I'm partly to blame for
Tylor's promotion as well.

00:17:16.882 --> 00:17:22.252
Actually, I feel like we
were somehow fated to meet.

00:17:22.988 --> 00:17:24.990
I have to reform Captain Tylor...

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:30.018
...and make the Soyokaze's crew
into real soldiers of the UPSF.

00:17:30.496 --> 00:17:34.091
I realized that
was my mission in life.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.002
That's why, despite
Admiral Mifune's objections...

00:17:37.002 --> 00:17:39.470
...I asked to be
assigned to this ship.

00:17:40.305 --> 00:17:43.172
Commander Star!
I'm so ashamed!

00:17:43.442 --> 00:17:48.311
To think I would consider
taking revenge on my own men!

00:17:54.153 --> 00:17:55.780
The enemy lies within!

00:17:55.854 --> 00:17:58.846
Now I see!
The enemy was myself!

00:17:59.625 --> 00:18:01.794
To doubt the military's style
of personnel management...

00:18:01.794 --> 00:18:04.262
...and have been so disappointed
with my men was inexcusable!

00:18:05.297 --> 00:18:09.028
Isn't it my duty to
cover my superiors' flaws...

00:18:09.635 --> 00:18:12.433
...and cure my men
of their rebellious nature?

00:18:12.971 --> 00:18:13.995
Lieutenant Yamamoto...

00:18:18.444 --> 00:18:20.503
Admiral Mifune, I...

00:18:20.846 --> 00:18:23.542
I have now defeated
the enemy within!

00:18:24.817 --> 00:18:26.307
Lieutenant! Emergency!

00:18:26.485 --> 00:18:27.076
What's wrong?!

00:18:27.186 --> 00:18:29.780
Trouble on the hangar deck,
sir! Get down there, fast!

00:18:49.875 --> 00:18:52.776
What's the meaning of this?!
Stop it at once!

00:18:53.178 --> 00:18:54.543
Lieutenant!

00:18:56.782 --> 00:18:59.273
What, you're still alive?

00:19:00.452 --> 00:19:02.044
Excuse me for living.

00:19:02.387 --> 00:19:04.685
Captain! Captain, please!

00:19:05.224 --> 00:19:07.055
Captain, please wake up!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.092
Mr. Tylor!

00:19:14.733 --> 00:19:16.860
Captain, there's trouble!

00:19:17.903 --> 00:19:18.699
What's wrong?

00:19:20.639 --> 00:19:21.571
What's this?

00:19:21.907 --> 00:19:23.675
Lieutenant Andressen left
that for you before.

00:19:23.675 --> 00:19:25.939
He said it was in
honor of your promotion.

00:19:26.245 --> 00:19:28.679
Really?
That was nice of him.

00:19:29.114 --> 00:19:30.046
Hm, let's see...

00:19:30.883 --> 00:19:33.418
This is heavy.
Wonder what's in it?

00:19:33.418 --> 00:19:35.113
Captain, never mind that!

00:19:35.387 --> 00:19:37.321
A war's broken out onboard!

00:19:37.456 --> 00:19:39.754
Huh? A war's started?

00:19:40.526 --> 00:19:44.563
Men, isn't it foolish for
fellow UPSF soldiers...

00:19:44.563 --> 00:19:48.431
...to fight each other
during a state of war?

00:19:49.268 --> 00:19:50.633
"The enemy lies within!"

00:19:51.136 --> 00:19:53.572
Surely you see the
meaning of those words!

00:19:53.572 --> 00:19:55.631
All right, all right.
Enough already.

00:19:55.707 --> 00:19:59.006
My hat's off to you,
First Officer Yamamoto.

00:19:59.478 --> 00:20:01.844
Oh? Is the war over already?

00:20:03.215 --> 00:20:05.012
So, who won?

00:20:06.418 --> 00:20:08.215
"Who won?!"

00:20:10.289 --> 00:20:12.780
Captain, look at this mess!

00:20:12.991 --> 00:20:15.789
Whoever won or lost
is beside the point!

00:20:16.228 --> 00:20:18.630
This may be the dumping
ground of the UPSF...

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:21.428
...but having our voyage start like
this makes me fear for our future!

00:20:22.167 --> 00:20:24.226
Looks like they really
went to town in here.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:27.600
Captain, please say
something to the crew!

00:20:27.873 --> 00:20:30.309
Tell them that, if they don't
stop these childish brawls...

00:20:30.309 --> 00:20:32.678
...and start behaving
like professionals...

00:20:32.678 --> 00:20:36.546
...then when it comes time to
show the Raalgon our true power...

00:20:37.282 --> 00:20:42.083
To show the Raalgon our true
power... we won't be able to...

00:20:42.254 --> 00:20:43.186
Captain!

00:20:43.755 --> 00:20:45.347
Please say something!

00:20:45.457 --> 00:20:48.290
Hm? Right...

00:20:48.894 --> 00:20:53.797
Captain, please! Give the
crew a clear and direct order!

00:20:56.034 --> 00:20:57.661
An order, huh?

00:21:00.505 --> 00:21:02.302
Okay. Do whatever you want.

00:21:02.674 --> 00:21:04.471
"Do whatever you?"

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:13.313
Captain!

00:21:13.485 --> 00:21:16.818
Right. Let's forget the rules
and just do whatever we want to.

00:21:17.456 --> 00:21:19.788
That's all.
The captain has spoken.

00:21:23.528 --> 00:21:27.828
You heard the captain. He said
do whatever we want, right, guys?

00:21:36.575 --> 00:21:37.906
Lieutenant Yamamoto...

00:21:38.477 --> 00:21:39.808
"The enemy within..."

00:21:40.212 --> 00:21:43.670
It isn't a weak heart or
mistrust of the military.

00:21:43.982 --> 00:21:46.416
The veteransâ€™ mutiny?
No, it isn't that, either!

00:21:48.687 --> 00:21:52.214
Justy Ueki Tylor... It's you!

00:21:52.858 --> 00:21:55.759
You are the enemy within!

00:22:12.744 --> 00:22:13.676
The Irresponsible Captain Tylor
Next Episode

00:22:15.681 --> 00:22:19.412
Love, strength, and discipline
lead to victory in battle.

00:22:19.584 --> 00:22:22.348
But does Tylor know
a truth beyond this?

00:22:22.721 --> 00:22:25.315
Next time, "Enemy!
Crisis! We Surrender!"

00:22:25.590 --> 00:22:26.491
Filming is Job 1!
Working hard for those who demand
the finest in image and sound
Watch for it.

